{
 "points": [
  {
   "id": "P1.1",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Language vague and analysis not rigorous.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.2",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Claim that diffusion models cannot learn posterior/score lacks rigorous support; ignores convergence theory.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.3",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Supporting arguments such as weighted-sum degradation are expected and not original.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P1.4",
   "reviewer": "P1",
   "text": "Natural inference section only reinterprets existing samplers; no new insights or methods.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.1",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "False 'first rigorous analysis' claim; existing literature on high-dimensional sparse setting not cited or compared.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.2",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Known proofs and diffusion/flow-matching equivalences presented without attribution.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.3",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Many vague, undefined statements and confusing notation; Sec. 4.1 lacks rigour (I_good/I_bad undefined).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.4",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Self guidance resembles uncited Autoguidance; no real contribution.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.5",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Proposed framework not defined with equations; Sec. 4.2 given only as bullet ideas.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.6",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Figure 5 confusing with undefined symbols.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.7",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "No empirical results for new framework or comparison with known samplers.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.8",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Appendix proofs imprecise: f_theta undefined, missing norms.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.9",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Flow matching discussion incorrect in general; ignores non-Gaussian paths.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.10",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Different flow-matching statistics due to noise schedule, not acknowledged.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.11",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Degradation is not equivalent to single-sample mean estimate; single-sample training works (VAEs).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P2.12",
   "reviewer": "P2",
   "text": "Learning ideal target is undesirable since it only reproduces training data; argument misguided.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P3.1",
   "reviewer": "P3",
   "text": "Main claim overstated: posterior concentration does not invalidate probabilistic formulation.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P3.2",
   "reviewer": "P3",
   "text": "Natural Inference Framework only re-expresses known samplers linearly; no new theory or algorithm.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P3.3",
   "reviewer": "P3",
   "text": "No experiments show the perspective improves understanding or performance.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.1",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Claim that models cannot learn high-dimensional distributions given without references or evidence.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.2",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Equation (15) unclear: expectation over x_t rather than x_0.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.3",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Figure 1 appears incorrect.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.4",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Lack of experiments in main text.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.5",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "No related work section.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.6",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Redundant content, including well-known score-matching equivalence proof.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.7",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Overuse of emphasized text.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.8",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Figure 5 cluttered and inadequately explained.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "P4.9",
   "reviewer": "P4",
   "text": "Formatting errors: missing caption periods, 'Eq. equation (1)'.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.1",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Analysis concerns empirical optimal denoiser, not learned network; network outputs never measured.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.2",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Inference from degenerate target to model failing to learn is asserted; conflates finite-sample and population targets.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.3",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Missing memorization/generalization and intrinsic-dimension literature; novelty overstated.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.4",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Posterior weight described as inversely proportional to distance, contradicting Gaussian form.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.5",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Notation slips in Eqs. 18-23.",
   "minor": true
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.6",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Standard posterior-mean regression reduction presented as contribution.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.7",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Degradation statistic close to tautological given sparsity relative to noise.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.8",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Degradation statistic implementation under-specified (softmax, threshold, t mapping, held-out points).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.9",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Only ImageNet analysed; no control datasets.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.10",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Conclusion contradicts practice where models generate novel content.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.11",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Predict-x0 understanding not new.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.12",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Frequency-domain explanation informal and untested.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.13",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Unified framework trivial consequence of linear sampler updates.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.14",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Equivalence only approximate; no error bounds or deviation tables.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.15",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Claim that Markov/SDE concepts are not needed overreaches.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.16",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Framework coverage incomplete: UniPC, predictor-corrector, stochastic samplers; DDPM breaks structure.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.17",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Linear multistep view already known; Self Guidance renaming adds no technical content.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.18",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Self Guidance quality enhancement argued by analogy only, untested.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.19",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "High-order solver explanation (5.1) lacks ablation.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.20",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Large-CFG explanation rests on one hand-picked example.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.21",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Sharpness control shown only qualitatively.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.22",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Over-enhancement attribution hypothetical; single qualitative verification without baseline.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.23",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Only quantitative result is CIFAR-10; no high-dimensional benchmarks.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.24",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "No seeds, confidence intervals or sample counts for FID.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.25",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Coefficient matrices tuned on same metric/model; no held-out check against overfitting.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.26",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Missing learned/searched solver baselines (UniPC, DPM-Solver-v3, LD3, AMED).",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.27",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Unusual baseline ordering suggests configuration issues; NFE accounting unclear.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.28",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "No reusable method; design principles are heuristics.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.29",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Title/abstract promise not addressed; sections loosely connected.",
   "minor": false
  },
  {
   "id": "Q1.30",
   "reviewer": "Q1",
   "text": "Numerous typos and inconsistencies.",
   "minor": true
  }
